<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lyciarch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lyciarch was the president of the Lycian League, the federation of the cities of ancient Lycia in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>. Elected each year by the league's assembly, he presided over its meetings and, in the Roman imperial period, over the provincial cult of the emperors. The office was held by the leading families of the region and is recorded in many inscriptions.</p></div>
